{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tp8wwkaEWQP1zvk8GGc9ve","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The new option added to the `--reset-offsets` action in `kafka-consumer-groups.sh` is **`--to-start-time`**, which uses the group creation timestamp as the reference point for `ListOffsets`.\\\\n\\\\nSupporting facts in time order:\\\\n\\\\n- **2026-04-10T17:41:33.000000Z** - The option was first proposed as `--by-start-time` in a message describing changes to `kafka-consumer-groups.sh`: \\\\\\\"*--reset-offsets gains a new --by-start-time option that uses the group creation timestamp as the reference point for ListOffsets.*\\\\\\\" [mail:4610133690d73a4c3ab59805]\\\\n- **2026-04-11T02:13:19.000000Z** - Jiunn-Yang confirmed the rename was adopted and applied to both tools: \\\\\\\"*Both --describe --state -verbose and --reset-offsets --to-start-time are now supported for streams groups as well.*\\\\\\\" [mail:a08165dfdf4f02a3371ea8d5]\\\\n- **2026-04-11T08:20:06.000000Z** - Andrew Schofield confirmed the pervasive rename across the KIP: \\\\\\\"*change all of the by_start_time, byStartTime and --by-start-time variants across the entire KIP to to_start_time, toStartTime and --to-start-time.*\\\\\\\" [mail:c93bd5f0d4ff49dcaab8ccdf]\\\\n- **2026-04-11T08:57:37.000000Z** - Jiunn-Yang agreed with the rename, explaining the `to_*` prefix conveys \\\\\\\"seek to a fixed point\\\\\\\" because the group creation time is an absolute, server-recorded timestamp. [mail:158dbb7f426e444843c14326]\\\\n- **2026-04-16T11:45:45.000000Z** - The final implementation was described: \\\\\\\"*--to-start-time uses AdminClient throughout the entire flow: describeConsumerGroups()/describeStreamsGroups() to fetch the group creation timestamp, ListOffsets to resolve offsets, and alterConsumerGroupOffsets.*\\\\\\\" [mail:8ddbf935ac780ddfcd014a27]\\\\n\\\\nWhat could not be determined: The exact Kafka version or release in which this 